IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g4-interpretation`
IMPORT `g4-nouns`
IMPORT `g4-art11-decision`
IMPORT `g4-art12-name`
IMPORT `g4-tests-fixtures`

-- g4-tests-art12-name.l4: tests for Article 12, whose expected values were decided from the Law's text BEFORE the encoding was run. The default reading is used throughout;
-- the other readings of F4.5, F4.7 and F4.8 are in g4-tests-forks.l4.

§ `Tests of Article 12`

§§ `Article 12(1) -- a name is undesirable if, in the Commissioner's opinion, one of four grounds applies`

-- No ground: the name is not undesirable.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 12(1) the name is undesirable` `the default reading` `the opinion that the name is unobjectionable`
-- (a): the same as, or too similar to, the name of any other registered charity: in the general section, in the restricted section.
#ASSERT `Art 12(1) the name is undesirable` `the default reading` (`the opinion that only the entries are the same or too similar` (LIST `the registered name of another charity, entered in the general section`))
#ASSERT `Art 12(1)(a) the name is the same as, or too similar to, the name of any other registered charity` `the default reading` (`the opinion that only the entries are the same or too similar` (LIST `the registered name of another charity, entered in the general section`))
#ASSERT `Art 12(1)(a) the name is the same as, or too similar to, the name of any other registered charity` `the default reading` (`the opinion that only the entries are the same or too similar` (LIST `the registered name of another charity, entered in the restricted section`))
-- "any OTHER registered charity": the charity's own name is not another's.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 12(1)(a) the name is the same as, or too similar to, the name of any other registered charity` `the default reading` (`the opinion that only the entries are the same or too similar` (LIST `the registered name of the charity itself`))
#ASSERT `Art 12(1)(a) the name is the same as, or too similar to, the name of any other registered charity` `the default reading` (`the opinion that only the entries are the same or too similar` (LIST `the registered name of the charity itself`, `the registered name of another charity, entered in the general section`))
-- No entry that the Commissioner thinks too similar: ground (a) fails.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 12(1)(a) the name is the same as, or too similar to, the name of any other registered charity` `the default reading` `the opinion that the name is unobjectionable`
-- (b), (c), (d): each alone makes the name undesirable, and only its own limb.
#ASSERT `Art 12(1) the name is undesirable` `the default reading` `the opinion that the name is likely to mislead the public`
#ASSERT `Art 12(1)(b) the name is likely to mislead the public as to the purpose, activities or identity of the entity` `the opinion that the name is likely to mislead the public`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 12(1)(c) the name gives the impression that the entity is connected to a person to which it is not connected` `the opinion that the name is likely to mislead the public`
#ASSERT `Art 12(1) the name is undesirable` `the default reading` `the opinion that the name gives the impression of a connection that does not exist`
#ASSERT `Art 12(1)(c) the name gives the impression that the entity is connected to a person to which it is not connected` `the opinion that the name gives the impression of a connection that does not exist`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 12(1)(d) the name is offensive` `the opinion that the name gives the impression of a connection that does not exist`
#ASSERT `Art 12(1) the name is undesirable` `the default reading` `the opinion that the name is offensive`
#ASSERT `Art 12(1)(d) the name is offensive` `the opinion that the name is offensive`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 12(1)(b) the name is likely to mislead the public as to the purpose, activities or identity of the entity` `the opinion that the name is offensive`

§§ `Article 12(2) -- the registered name and the registration number`

-- (a) enter the name of the entity in the register as the registered name.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 12(2)(a) the Commissioner must enter the name of the entity in the register as the registered name` `a Jersey company that has applied` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 60)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 12(2)(a) the Commissioner must enter the name of the entity in the register as the registered name` `a Jersey company that has applied` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES (`Act under Article 12` OF `the Commissioner`, (`enter the name of the entity in the register as the registered name` "Hope Foundation Limited")) AT 5

-- Entering some other name is not entering the name of the entity: the duty stands.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 12(2)(a) the Commissioner must enter the name of the entity in the register as the registered name` `a Jersey company that has applied` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES (`Act under Article 12` OF `the Commissioner`, (`enter the name of the entity in the register as the registered name` "Hope Foundation")) AT 5

-- The Commissioner has not registered the entity: nothing is owed.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 12(2)(a) the Commissioner must enter the name of the entity in the register as the registered name` `a Jersey company that has applied` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 60)

-- (b) allocate a number in respect of the registration, and enter it: whatever number the Commissioner allocates.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 12(2)(b) the Commissioner must allocate a registration number and enter it in the register` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 60)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 12(2)(b) the Commissioner must allocate a registration number and enter it in the register` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES (`Act under Article 12` OF `the Commissioner`, (`allocate a registration number and enter it in the register` "JC-2026-001")) AT 5

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 12(2)(b) the Commissioner must allocate a registration number and enter it in the register` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 60)

-- (a) and (b) together: one done leaves the other standing; both done discharges.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 12(2) the Commissioner must enter the registered name and allocate and enter a number` `a Jersey company that has applied` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES (`Act under Article 12` OF `the Commissioner`, (`enter the name of the entity in the register as the registered name` "Hope Foundation Limited")) AT 5

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 12(2) the Commissioner must enter the registered name and allocate and enter a number` `a Jersey company that has applied` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES (`Act under Article 12` OF `the Commissioner`, (`enter the name of the entity in the register as the registered name` "Hope Foundation Limited")) AT 5
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES (`Act under Article 12` OF `the Commissioner`, (`allocate a registration number and enter it in the register` "JC-2026-001")) AT 6

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 12(2) the Commissioner must enter the registered name and allocate and enter a number` `a Jersey company that has applied` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 60)

§§ `Article 12(3) to (6) -- changing the registered name or adding an alternative`

-- (3) a registered charity may apply; the permission stays open.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 12(3) a registered charity may apply for permission to change its registered name or to add an alternative registered name` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 365)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 12(3) a registered charity may apply for permission to change its registered name or to add an alternative registered name` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES (`Act under Article 12` OF `a registered charity`, (`apply for permission to change the registered name or to add an alternative registered name` `a change of the registered name`)) AT 10

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 12(3) a registered charity may apply for permission to change its registered name or to add an alternative registered name` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES (`Act under Article 12` OF `a registered charity`, (`apply for permission to change the registered name or to add an alternative registered name` `the addition of an alternative registered name`)) AT 10

-- An entity that is not a registered charity has no such permission.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 12(3) a registered charity may apply for permission to change its registered name or to add an alternative registered name` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 365)

-- (4) the Commissioner must refuse permission if a ground of Article 12(1) applies to the proposed name.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 12(4) the Commissioner must refuse permission to change or add a name` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 60)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 12(4) the Commissioner must refuse permission to change or add a name` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES (`Act under Article 12` OF `the Commissioner`, `refuse permission to change the registered name or to add an alternative registered name`) AT 10

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 12(4) the Commissioner must refuse permission to change or add a name` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 60)

#ASSERT `Art 12(4) what the Commissioner must do on the application for permission` TRUE EQUALS JUST (`Decision of the Commissioner` OF `whether to permit a change or addition of registered name, Article 12(4)`, `the Commissioner refuses`)
-- Where no ground applies the Law states no duty to grant: the decision is the Commissioner's, and the model answers NOTHING.
#ASSERT `Art 12(4) what the Commissioner must do on the application for permission` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (5) if permission is granted and the charity notifies that it has changed or added the name accordingly, the Commissioner must enter the name.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 12(5) the Commissioner must enter the new or alternative registered name` TRUE "Hope Trust" `the addition of an alternative registered name` TRUE "Hope Trust" `the addition of an alternative registered name` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 60)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 12(5) the Commissioner must enter the new or alternative registered name` TRUE "Hope Trust" `the addition of an alternative registered name` TRUE "Hope Trust" `the addition of an alternative registered name` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES (`Act under Article 12` OF `the Commissioner`, (`enter the new or alternative registered name in the register` "Hope Trust" `the addition of an alternative registered name`)) AT 20

-- Entering the name as a change of the registered name, when it was added as an alternative, is not what was notified.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 12(5) the Commissioner must enter the new or alternative registered name` TRUE "Hope Trust" `the addition of an alternative registered name` TRUE "Hope Trust" `the addition of an alternative registered name` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES (`Act under Article 12` OF `the Commissioner`, (`enter the new or alternative registered name in the register` "Hope Trust" `a change of the registered name`)) AT 20

-- Permission not granted: nothing is owed.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 12(5) the Commissioner must enter the new or alternative registered name` FALSE "Hope Trust" `the addition of an alternative registered name` TRUE "Hope Trust" `the addition of an alternative registered name` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 60)

-- Permission granted but the charity has not notified the Commissioner: nothing is owed.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 12(5) the Commissioner must enter the new or alternative registered name` TRUE "Hope Trust" `the addition of an alternative registered name` FALSE "Hope Trust" `the addition of an alternative registered name` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 60)

-- The charity notified a different name than the one permitted: not "accordingly".
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 12(5) the Commissioner must enter the new or alternative registered name` TRUE "Hope Trust" `the addition of an alternative registered name` TRUE "Hope Trust Jersey" `the addition of an alternative registered name` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 60)

-- The charity changed its registered name where the permission was to add an alternative: not "accordingly".
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 12(5) the Commissioner must enter the new or alternative registered name` TRUE "Hope Trust" `the addition of an alternative registered name` TRUE "Hope Trust" `a change of the registered name` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 60)

-- (6) if a registered charity reports a matter relating to its registered name under Article 13(6)(b), the Commissioner may require it to apply to change its registered name.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 12(6) the Commissioner may require the charity to apply to change its registered name` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 365)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 12(6) the Commissioner may require the charity to apply to change its registered name` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES (`Act under Article 12` OF `the Commissioner`, `require the charity to apply to change its registered name`) AT 10

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 12(6) the Commissioner may require the charity to apply to change its registered name` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 365)

-- The decision, for Article 33(2)(c): the Commissioner requires, or does not; NOTHING where the charity reported nothing.
#ASSERT `Art 12(6) the decision of the Commissioner on whether to require the charity to apply` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 12(6) the decision of the Commissioner on whether to require the charity to apply` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 12(6) the decision of the Commissioner on whether to require the charity to apply` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST (`Decision of the Commissioner` OF `whether to require a charity to apply to change its registered name, Article 12(6)`, `the Commissioner does what was sought or proposed`)
#ASSERT `Art 12(6) the decision of the Commissioner on whether to require the charity to apply` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (`Decision of the Commissioner` OF `whether to require a charity to apply to change its registered name, Article 12(6)`, `the Commissioner refuses`)

§§ `Article 12(7) -- the names a registered charity may use`

`the charity registered as Hope Foundation Limited with the alternative name Hope Trust` MEANS `Registered charity` WITH
    entity IS `a Jersey company that is a registered charity`
    `registration number` IS "JC-2026-001"
    `registered name` IS "Hope Foundation Limited"
    `alternative registered names` IS LIST "Hope Trust"
    `date registered` IS YMD 2026 4 2
    `date deregistered` IS NOTHING
    `registered charitable purposes` IS EMPTY
    `registered public benefit statement` IS "Relief of poverty in Jersey"
    `is an organized religious charity` IS FALSE

-- a name used, with the names the charity has given up, whether it is related to a registered name, and the Commissioner's opinion of it in the context in which it is used.
`the use of the registered name` MEANS `Name used by a registered charity` WITH
    `name used` IS "Hope Foundation Limited"
    `previous registered names of the charity` IS EMPTY
    `related to one of the charity's registered names` IS FALSE
    `undesirable within Article 12(1) in the context in which it is used, in the opinion of the Commissioner` IS FALSE

`the use of the alternative registered name` MEANS `Name used by a registered charity` WITH
    `name used` IS "Hope Trust"
    `previous registered names of the charity` IS EMPTY
    `related to one of the charity's registered names` IS FALSE
    `undesirable within Article 12(1) in the context in which it is used, in the opinion of the Commissioner` IS FALSE

`the use of a related name that is not undesirable in its context` MEANS `Name used by a registered charity` WITH
    `name used` IS "Hope Foundation Appeal"
    `previous registered names of the charity` IS EMPTY
    `related to one of the charity's registered names` IS TRUE
    `undesirable within Article 12(1) in the context in which it is used, in the opinion of the Commissioner` IS FALSE

`the use of a related name that is undesirable in its context` MEANS `Name used by a registered charity` WITH
    `name used` IS "Hope Foundation Appeal"
    `previous registered names of the charity` IS EMPTY
    `related to one of the charity's registered names` IS TRUE
    `undesirable within Article 12(1) in the context in which it is used, in the opinion of the Commissioner` IS TRUE

`the use of an unrelated name that is not undesirable` MEANS `Name used by a registered charity` WITH
    `name used` IS "Acme Charity"
    `previous registered names of the charity` IS EMPTY
    `related to one of the charity's registered names` IS FALSE
    `undesirable within Article 12(1) in the context in which it is used, in the opinion of the Commissioner` IS FALSE

-- (a) its registered name or one of its registered names.
#ASSERT `Art 12(7) the name used is permitted` `the default reading` `the charity registered as Hope Foundation Limited with the alternative name Hope Trust` `the use of the registered name`
#ASSERT `Art 12(7) the name used is permitted` `the default reading` `the charity registered as Hope Foundation Limited with the alternative name Hope Trust` `the use of the alternative registered name`
#ASSERT `Art 12(7)(a) the name used is its registered name or one of its registered names` `the default reading` `the charity registered as Hope Foundation Limited with the alternative name Hope Trust` `the use of the alternative registered name`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 12(7)(a) the name used is its registered name or one of its registered names` `the default reading` `the charity registered as Hope Foundation Limited with the alternative name Hope Trust` `the use of a related name that is not undesirable in its context`
-- (b) another name that is related to such a name and is not, in the Commissioner's opinion, undesirable in the context in which it is used.
#ASSERT `Art 12(7) the name used is permitted` `the default reading` `the charity registered as Hope Foundation Limited with the alternative name Hope Trust` `the use of a related name that is not undesirable in its context`
#ASSERT `Art 12(7)(b) the name used is related to a registered name and is not undesirable in its context` `the use of a related name that is not undesirable in its context`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 12(7) the name used is permitted` `the default reading` `the charity registered as Hope Foundation Limited with the alternative name Hope Trust` `the use of a related name that is undesirable in its context`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 12(7) the name used is permitted` `the default reading` `the charity registered as Hope Foundation Limited with the alternative name Hope Trust` `the use of an unrelated name that is not undesirable`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 12(7)(b) the name used is related to a registered name and is not undesirable in its context` `the use of an unrelated name that is not undesirable`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 12(7)(b) the name used is related to a registered name and is not undesirable in its context` `the use of a related name that is undesirable in its context`

-- The prohibition run against the names used. A permitted name breaches nothing.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 12(7) a registered charity must not use a name other than a registered or related name` `the default reading` `the charity registered as Hope Foundation Limited with the alternative name Hope Trust` `the use of the registered name` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES (`Act under Article 12` OF `a registered charity`, (`use a name` "Hope Foundation Limited")) AT 5

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 12(7) a registered charity must not use a name other than a registered or related name` `the default reading` `the charity registered as Hope Foundation Limited with the alternative name Hope Trust` `the use of a related name that is not undesirable in its context` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES (`Act under Article 12` OF `a registered charity`, (`use a name` "Hope Foundation Appeal")) AT 5

-- A name that is neither registered nor a related name that is acceptable in its context: using it is a breach.
-- EXPECT: BREACH
#TRACE `Art 12(7) a registered charity must not use a name other than a registered or related name` `the default reading` `the charity registered as Hope Foundation Limited with the alternative name Hope Trust` `the use of an unrelated name that is not undesirable` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES (`Act under Article 12` OF `a registered charity`, (`use a name` "Acme Charity")) AT 5

-- EXPECT: BREACH
#TRACE `Art 12(7) a registered charity must not use a name other than a registered or related name` `the default reading` `the charity registered as Hope Foundation Limited with the alternative name Hope Trust` `the use of a related name that is undesirable in its context` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES (`Act under Article 12` OF `a registered charity`, (`use a name` "Hope Foundation Appeal")) AT 5

-- Article 12(7) binds "a registered charity" (Article 1: an entity entered in the general or the restricted section). An entity that has been deregistered is in the historic section and is not bound.
#ASSERT `Art 12(7) the entity is a registered charity` `the charity registered as Hope Foundation Limited with the alternative name Hope Trust`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 12(7) the entity is a registered charity` `the register entry of the charity that has been deregistered`
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 12(7) a registered charity must not use a name other than a registered or related name` `the default reading` `the register entry of the charity that has been deregistered` `the use of an unrelated name that is not undesirable` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES (`Act under Article 12` OF `a registered charity`, (`use a name` "Acme Charity")) AT 5

-- The prohibition stands for as long as the name is not used, and a different name used breaches nothing under it.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 12(7) a registered charity must not use a name other than a registered or related name` `the default reading` `the charity registered as Hope Foundation Limited with the alternative name Hope Trust` `the use of an unrelated name that is not undesirable` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 365)

-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 12(7) a registered charity must not use a name other than a registered or related name` `the default reading` `the charity registered as Hope Foundation Limited with the alternative name Hope Trust` `the use of an unrelated name that is not undesirable` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES (`Act under Article 12` OF `a registered charity`, (`use a name` "Hope Foundation Limited")) AT 5
